# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE — project "Vasilevsa"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Template. Copy to .env and fill in the real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The values are in the Supabase dashboard under
#   Project Settings -> API
#
# Restart the dev server after editing .env — Astro reads it at startup.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- safe in the browser -----------------------------------------------------
# The PUBLIC_ prefix tells Astro these may be inlined into client-side code.
# The anon key is designed to be public: it grants nothing by itself and every
# request it makes is filtered by Row Level Security.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# --- optional: the origin this app is reached at ----------------------------
# Only the password-recovery email needs this — it is the origin Supabase is
# told to send the link back to. Leave it blank and the app uses the origin of
# the request, which is correct on localhost and correct on any host that is
# not behind a proxy rewriting the Host header.
#
# Whatever it ends up being, the same origin must be listed in the Supabase
# dashboard under Authentication -> URL Configuration -> Redirect URLs. An
# unlisted redirect is not refused — it is silently replaced by the project's
# Site URL, which is how a reset link ends up pointing at the wrong port.
#
#   local development   http://localhost:4321
#   production          https://the-real-domain

PUBLIC_SITE_URL=


# --- server only — NEVER give this a PUBLIC_ prefix --------------------------
# The service-role key bypasses Row Level Security completely. Anyone holding
# it can read and delete every row in the project.
#
#   - never commit it (.env is already in .gitignore)
#   - never paste it into a component, a <script> block or a chat window
#   - in production set it in the host's environment panel, not in a file
#
# Leave it blank until something on the server actually needs it.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
